  "proof": "For triangle vertices a,b,c and x=lambda_a*a+lambda_b*b+lambda_c*c, distance(x,a)<=lambda_b*distance(b,a)+lambda_c*distance(c,a)<=2rho. If distance(q,mesh)<=epsilon, choosing a closest surface point x gives distance(q,P)<=distance(q,x)+distance(x,a)<=epsilon+2rho. Thus distance(q,P)>epsilon+2rho is impossible to cover within epsilon by any allowed triangle mesh using P. Using ALL points only weakens this bound. Reachability is necessary, not sufficient. Bound concerns sampled surface-distance completeness, NOT projected silhouette coverage.",
